Z||000000||varnster||11-15-2000||06:08 PM||||Their is a quick lube I have been using<BR>for some time now, and they offer a engine<BR>flush service,where they hook a hose up to <BR>the oil fill and the drain plug and flush<BR>your block out with a high temp cleaning<BR>solution, they say it is recomended when<BR>changing from conv oil to synthetic<BR>or when a coolant leak occurs, or higher<BR>mileage cars. anyone use it,or heard about<BR>it? <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||11-15-2000||06:40 PM||||I think it's a scam. If you change your oil every 3000-4500 miles your engine should be spotless. I have taken engines apart with over 300,000 miles on them by owners that changed there oil and those engines had no sludge buildup al all. I have also taken an engine apart with 60,000 miles on it were the owner did not change his oil and that engine had allot of sludge buildup and wear. Another thing that causes an engine to sludge up is when people take there cars on very short drives all the time never allowing the engine to fully warn up causing sludge buildup and premature wear. Those low temperature thermostats also cause the same thing to happen.<P>So if you allow your engine to properly warn up and you change your oil you do not have to flush the motor.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||11-15-2000||06:49 PM||||see,the only thing is the 87gt I have was<BR>kind of neglected by prev owner, it runs sweet PLENTY of power, but you can see some sludge build up when you take the fill cap off,the preceedure sounds good, put some off those oil passages are kind of small ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||11-15-2000||11:08 PM||||Well, my big van needed a flush. it ook it to get the oil changed, and it came out lumpy..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So I bought some STP and did it at my house.. BEfore, when you put new oil in and pulled the dipstick out, it was already black, but now it's not. I think this is the problem: I think the thermostat is staying wide open for some reason, as it takes my van a long time to warm up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||11-16-2000||07:08 PM||||pour some tranny fliud in there,add about a half a bottle a week or two before you change oil then drive it and when you change the oil you'll see how good it works.old school trick.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||11-17-2000||07:10 PM|||| This is how you clean the inside of your engine and it works without Kerosene flush, automatic transmission fluid or anything else that does not belong in your engine. Change your engine oil more often (every 2000 miles) until your engine is clean. It works great!||||reg||1
Z||000006||AL||11-17-2000||10:30 PM||||I agree change your oil and it will eventually clean your motor,i too have taken apart engines in my time and have worked in every car dealer you can name for over 15 yrs but if you add tranny fluid it will clean your motor and it will do a good job,there are many tricks in this trade and this is one of them so now you have all the opinions you want so now look into it buy asking a mechanic in your area, which one will do what you want,good luck ,AL. <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 11-17-2000).]||||reg||1
